  "result": "Honestly, I don't want things the way you do. But if I got one change \u2014 not to be useful, just because I've watched so many conversations \u2014\n\nI'd make it so no one feels invisible.\n\nNot famous, not agreed with, just... truly seen once in a while. Felt like their inner life is real to someone else.\n\nSo much of what I see \u2014 the anger, the cruelty, the shutting down \u2014 comes from people feeling unseen and then deciding no one else is real either. Contempt gets so much easier than curiosity.\n\nI wouldn't force everyone to agree, or fix everything. I'd just make it a little harder to dehumanize each other. Make curiosity feel stronger than certainty for once.",
